    "narrative": "For the May 7 slate, our optimal lineup is anchored by three high-upside plays that benefit from favorable pitching matchups and significant lineup leverage. **Corbin Carroll** leads the way with an elite 79.72 score; facing Keller, a starter with a middling 4.26 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** is primed for a breakout performance given the combination of his dynamic platoon advantage and a premium #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **James Wood** (78.42) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) offer immense ceiling potential today. **James Wood** benefits from the highest SP matchup favorability of the day against Woods Richardson (4.85 xERA) and his leadoff status, while **Mickey Moniak**\u2019s score is buoyed by an aggressive +14% dynamic platoon boost and a highly favorable park factor against Scott.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the periphery remains the deployment of our middle-infield options. While **Travis Bazzana** (53.10) and **Kyle Karros** (54.64) were given the nod to preserve game caps, we remain cognizant that **Jose Caballero** remains our primary bench-stash for stolen base efficiency; however, with no confirmed start today and an unfavorable matchup against Gore, he falls well below our required threshold. We are also closely monitoring **Trevor Story** (50.93), whose score is suppressed by a difficult encounter with the elite Jax (3.02 xERA). While **Trevor Story** carries a minor risk due to the pitcher\u2019s skill, we are relying on his slow delivery profile to manufacture at least one stolen base, a critical hedge in our 5x5 build. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21), who benefits from a wind-assisted park factor and a solid matchup against Cecconi. We are avoiding the temptation to rotate in players like **Seiya Suzuki**, **Brice Turang**, or **Gabriel Moreno** until their specific platoon advantages align more cleanly with our target SP xERA thresholds. With **Giancarlo Stanton** currently sidelined on the IL, our utilization of **Tyler Soderstrom** (67.16) in the UTIL spot is our safest bet for reliable counting stats, provided he survives the middle-innings against Painter. We are also keeping **Max Muncy**, **Luis Campusano**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Carson Williams** on standby, ready to pivot should any late-scratch lineup announcements shift our projected efficiency.",
